Lubellion the Searing Dragon\" once per turn."},"72167543":{"role":"DARK · Rank 4 · ATK 2100","quick":"Overlay a surviving Rank 3 or lower Xyz in Main Phase 2 to build the Zeus stack.","caution":"The alternate route is Main Phase 2 only. Do not summon under the Mikanko restriction."},"73819701":{"role":"Branded engine","quick":"(This card is always treated as \"Fallen of Albaz\".)\r\nIf this card is in your hand: You can send 1 monster that mentions \"Fallen of Albaz\" from your Extra Deck to the GY; Special Summon this card, also you cannot Special Summon from the Extra Deck for the rest of this turn, except Level 8 Fusion or Synchro Monsters. If this card is Normal or Special Summoned: You can Special Summon 1 \"Ecclesia\" monster from your hand, Deck, or GY. You can only use each effect of \"Fallen of the White Dragon\" once per turn."},"74405783":{"role":"Extra Deck tool","quick":"1 Level 4 Tuner + 1+ non-Tuners\r\nIf this card is Synchro Summoned: You can add 1 Level 4 or 8 Spellcaster monster whose ATK equals its own DEF from your Deck or GY to your hand. You can target 1 face-up card on the field; negate its effects, then if you have an \"Ecclesia\" monster or \"Fallen of Albaz\" in your GY, you can destroy that card. You can only use each effect of \"The Three Champions of Swordsoul\" once per turn."},"74677422":{"role":"Branded engine","quick":"''A ferocious dragon with a deadly attack.''"},"75147529":{"role":"Sky Striker","quick":"Uses two monsters including an Ace; excellent for clearing a monster taken by Widow Anchor."},"76072561":{"role":"Sky Striker","quick":"On Special Summon, search a Striker Spell. Zero can search or use the Tribute deployment effect that turn—not both."},"76666602":{"role":"Extra Deck tool","quick":"\"Fallen of Albaz\" + 1 LIGHT or DARK monster + 1 Effect Monster\r\nWhile an \"Ecclesia\" monster is on the field or in either GY, this card gains 500 ATK, also it is unaffected by other cards' effects. You can only use each of the following effects of \"The Dragon that Devours the Dogma\" once per turn. If this card is Special Summoned: You can shuffle up to 2 cards from any GY(s) and/or banishment into the Deck. During the End Phase, if this card is in the GY because it was sent there this turn: You can add 1 \"Dogmatika\" or \"Tri-Brigade\" card from your Deck to your hand."},"78114463":{"role":"Sky Striker","quick":"Can be activated the turn it was Set by revealing another Set Trap; choose the LP mode deliberately."},"78199891":{"role":"Trap","quick":"While you control a Mikanko, target a face-up monster and equip an Equip Spell from Deck that can legally equip to it.","caution":"You need a Mikanko already on field. Rondo can equip to an opponent’s monster and immediately take it."},"79912449":{"role":"Spell","quick":"Equip an opposing monster, then control it while you control a Mikanko. It remains equipped under your control.","caution":"Both players are prevented from activating that monster’s effects while you control it. Losing Rondo sends the equipped monster to GY."},"80044027":{"role":"Equip Spell","quick":"Summons a Mikanko from hand or GY and equips it. Can optionally put a negated monster from their GY back on their field as a damage target.","caution":"Only one activation per turn. The optional opposing revival requires a legal GY target. Equipping it through Ohime is not the same as activating its summon effect."},"80843006":{"role":"Extra Deck tool","quick":"1 Spellcaster monster + 1 non-Spellcaster monster\r\nYou can target 1 face-up monster on the field and declare 1 Attribute; it becomes that Attribute. During your opponent's Main Phase (Quick Effect): You can Fusion Summon 1 Fusion Monster from your Extra Deck, by banishing this card you control and monsters from your field or GY as material. If this card is in your GY: You can declare 1 Attribute; this card in the GY becomes that Attribute until the end of this turn. You can only use each effect of \"Mixousia the Confounder\" once per turn."},"81196066":{"role":"2 Lunalights. If Fusion Summoned, searches Luna Light Perfume; can target another Lunalight card you control to return it to hand/Extra Deck, then optionally Special Summon a Lunalight from hand. Its GY banish reduces opposing ATK by original DEF.","quick":"21442"},"81260679":{"role":"LIGHT · Level 6 · ATK 0","quick":"Reveals herself to search a Mikanko card, then discards. Preparation finds her. Ceremony can bring her onto the field, where she can equip a suitable GY Equip Spell as a Quick Effect.","caution":"The discard happens during resolution, not as activation cost. She is Level 6, not a Rank 3 material. Ceremony does not properly Ritual Summon her."},"81439173":{"role":"GY access","quick":"Send one monster from Deck to GY. Limited to one."},"82344137":{"role":"Branded engine","quick":"You can reveal this card and 1 Spell/Trap in your hand; until the end of the next turn, neither player can activate cards or effects in response to the activation of cards, or effects of cards, with the revealed Spell/Trap's name. If this card is sent from the hand or field to the GY by a Spell/Trap effect: You can Special Summon this card. If this card is Special Summoned from the GY: You can take control of 1 monster your opponent controls with the highest ATK (your choice, if tied). You can only use each effect of \"Phara the Primordial Goddess\" once per turn."},"82489470":{"role":"Branded engine","quick":"When a monster declares an attack: You can Special Summon this card from your hand, and if you do, negate that attack, then, if you control a Fusion Monster that mentions \"Fallen of Albaz\" as material, you can destroy the monster that declared that attack. If a monster is banished face-up (except during the Damage Step): You can banish this card from your field or GY; Special Summon 1 LIGHT Spellcaster monster from your hand or GY whose ATK equals its own DEF. You can only use this effect of \"The Golden Swordsoul\" once per turn."